WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:00.934
John.

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.669
Well, Karim Khan was keen to tell us

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.403
that this is really

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.238
just the first step in

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.440
what promises to be a long journey.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.608
The arrest warrants

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.876
that were given out today

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.112
for President Putin and also for the

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:13.380
Russian high

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.581
commissioner for children,

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.616
Maria Liv over Bill Oliver.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.053
These are just the first to essentially

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.521
there may be more coming.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.223
There may be other areas

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.924
that they will be exploring.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.659
There is no shortage

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.294
of alleged war crimes

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.764
that have taken place in Ukraine.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:33.033
The prosecutor's office

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.200
here from the ICC

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.504
have made multiple trips to Ukraine,

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.873
but they were keen really to stress

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:43.009
the importance of this historic day.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.445
Take a look.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:48.448
There are many different war crimes

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.216
or potential war crimes

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.318
that we've seen playing out in Ukraine,

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.954
whether it's the bombing of the theater

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:55.722
in Mariupol,

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.157
where people were sheltering,

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.825
civilians were sheltering,

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.960
whether it's the atrocities of Butcher.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:05.265
Why did you decide to pursue this line

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:07.100
of prosecution first?

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.101
We are absolutely right.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.804
Firstly, I stated when I was outside St

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:12.272
Andrew's Church

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.641
in Russia about a year ago,

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.242
just less than a year ago,

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.911
that Ukraine is a crime scene

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.080
and there's many terrible allegations

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.081
that have been received,

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:22.148
and we're analyzing them

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.450
and reviewing them.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.718
But before my election as prosecutor,

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.555
before I started in June of 2021,

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.023
I also identified

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.658
the crimes against all crimes

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:33.193
affecting children

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.727
are under investigated

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:35.662
and under-reported.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.497
And this is why when you look at the

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:38.531
the factual matrix,

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.033
the actual evidence that we received,

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.435
it was only right and appropriate

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.304
to focus on the most vulnerable

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.339
parts of our society, which are children.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.174
We understand that

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:51.044
over Belova is the Russian Commissioner

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:51.778
for children.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.580
She's been very vocal and visible

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.115
in her role.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.817
How did you take the next step also

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.786
in terms of pushing for the prosecution

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.287
of President Putin himself?

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.356
And how unusual is that?

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.058
Well, I've said

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.493
repeatedly over the last year

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:08.228
that we don't start with targets,

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.163
that we start with the evidence.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.264
We investigate

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.765
incriminating and

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.400
exonerating evidence equally.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.902
We want to find the truth.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.937
We are statutorily required

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.339
to get to the truth.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.241
And we, as I said,

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.643
started looking at a range of ways,

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.345
spectrum of allegations.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.946
But the evidence was quite clear

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.982
because what has been said publicly

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.184
from those individuals,

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:32.585
what has become available

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.522
from publicly available sources, and also

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.091
the result of our direct investigations

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.827
ourselves, cooperation with other states

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.061
and also Ukraine,

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:42.962
that this

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:43.830
these crimes appear

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.031
to have been committed.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.566
And one follows the evidence.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.935
And the simple reality is

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.670
these crimes have not been hidden.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.605
It's the first time in history

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:53.773
any head of state

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:54.874
of the permanent members

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.042
of the five permanent members

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.677
of the Security Council

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.646
has had a warrant of arrest

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.980
issued by independent

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.482
and impartial judges.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.817
It shouldn't give us any celebration.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.153
It's a matter of real regret

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.189
that we've had to do this.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:10.890
The evidence compelled us to move

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.091
in this manner.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.093
It's a historic moment, certainly.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.662
But will we ever see

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.797
President Putin in the dock?

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.199
Well, the president of the court

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:20.033
made it very clear

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.235
our job is to independently

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:22.902
and impartially,

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.504
without any political motivations

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:25.838
or agendas.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.074
Look at apply the law to the facts,

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.509
the facts that have been verified,

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.643
that have been

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.545
independently collected

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:35.081
and rigorously analyzed.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.283
Now it's for others to decide

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.818
whether or not

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.820
arrest opportunities are available

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.355
and if so, to enforce them.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:45.225
The first is many thought

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.460
it was impossible

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.895
that powerful leaders like

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:50.663
former President

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:51.497
Milosevic,

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:54.500
former President Charles Taylor,

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.636
Karadzic, Mladic and John,

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:58.338
commander of Rwanda,

00:03:58.338 --> 00:04:00.540
accused the pan of Cambodia.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.775
The list goes on.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.143
He said Habré

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.945
would ever be subjected

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.213
to the rule of law,

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.314
and yet they were

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.917
some of them are in custody.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.585
And, of course, award is back with us.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:13.253
Clarissa.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.954
No expectation, obviously,

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.456
that Vladimir Putin

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.891
would surrender or be arrested.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:21.361
So did the ICC give you a sense

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:25.632
of how it intends to proceed legally?

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:27.634
Well,
that's the question

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.503
really, John, because the ICC can't trial

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:31.604
can't have a trial

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.640
of someone in absentia.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.074
But what they can do,

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.744
according to prosecutor Khan and again,

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:38.177
this hasn't

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.479
been done historically,

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:41.648
but there is legal precedent for it

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:45.351
is what they call a confirmation hearing

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:46.853
in absence.

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:49.389
And that would essentially allow

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:51.991
for the evidence to be preserved

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:55.528
in a judicial setting in a timely way,

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.996
paving the way

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.032
for some potential future trial.

00:04:59.032 --> 00:04:59.999
What they have seen.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.835
Traditionally the ICC is that

00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:04.570
very rarely do people

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:05.905
charged with war crimes

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:08.141
actually come to face justice

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:11.311
until those wars have reached an end.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.412
And whichever side is

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:14.781
victorious gets to choose who ends up

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:18.251
facing trial at the ICC.

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.485
So what they want to do,

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.621
at least with this possibility

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:22.655
of the confirmation

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.023
hearing, is ensure

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:24.891
that that evidence

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:26.926
is put out there in a timely manner,

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:30.396
that victims of these alleged atrocities

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:30.930
are able

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.899
to still have their day in court,

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:34.100
even if it might be

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.535
quite some time before

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:37.770
you would potentially see

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.605
President Vladimir Putin

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.407
appearing on trial, though,

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.076
I think for the moment that does

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:45.511
seem like a very distant prospect, John.

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:46.379
Of course, to stay with us,

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:47.580
I want to bring in Matthew Chance

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.414
and Ivan Watson.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:49.782
Ivan, what has the reaction

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:51.784
been from the Ukrainian government

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.152
to these arrest warrants?

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:56.823
John, the Ukrainian government

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:58.091
has been applauding

00:05:58.091 --> 00:05:59.025
this decision,

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.193
the arrest warrant issued

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:02.295
by the International Criminal Court.

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:04.530
According to government statistics,

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.498
they say that

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:09.235
some 16,226 Ukrainian children,

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:11.637
the government believes, have been taken

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:14.674
and deported to Russia since the start

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:16.275
of the Russian invasion

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:18.511
a bit more than a year ago.

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:19.112
Take a listen

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:19.545
to what

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:20.947
the Ukrainian president, Volodymyr

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:22.915
Zelensky, had to say about this,

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:24.984
which he calls an historic decision

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.555
resulting in the U.S.

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:31.657
separating children from their families,

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:33.826
depriving them of any opportunity

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.561
to contact their relatives.

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:37.263
Hiding children in Russia.

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:39.832
Dispersing them to remote regions.

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:42.268
All this is obvious Russian state policy,

00:06:42.435 --> 00:06:44.704
state decisions and state evil,

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.205
which begins

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:49.642
with the first official of the state.

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:53.045
So, you know, another top Ukrainian

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:54.614
official has just called this

00:06:54.614 --> 00:06:56.215
a first step.

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:57.750
Meanwhile, the top prosecutor

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.317
in the country,

00:06:58.317 --> 00:06:59.318
he says that he hopes

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:01.521
that this will make other world leaders

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:03.423
think twice about in the future,

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.358
shaking hands with Vladimir Putin

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.059
or sitting down at the negotiating

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:07.860
table with him

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:08.761
now that he's

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:11.030
effectively become a suspected

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:12.532
war criminal.

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:15.201
Well, the ICC move is important.

00:07:15.201 --> 00:07:16.469
It's also important,

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:18.504
I think, to to understand

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.541
that the Ukrainian judicial system

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:23.042
that police here on the ground,

00:07:23.042 --> 00:07:24.010
that investigators

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:25.111
and prosecutors,

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:27.814
that they are also separately actively

00:07:27.814 --> 00:07:28.981
gathering evidence

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:31.350
for their own cases to accuse

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:34.654
Russian military commanders

00:07:34.654 --> 00:07:36.923
and individual Russian soldiers

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.193
of alleged war crime so that after

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:41.861
every kind of rocket strike

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:43.963
or artillery strike

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:46.232
on a Ukrainian city or town,

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:48.301
after every death of a civilian.

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:50.470
You have police coming in later,

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:51.571
if it's at all

00:07:51.571 --> 00:07:52.939
safe in an area,

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:53.973
gathering evidence

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:56.209
and putting their own cases together

00:07:56.409 --> 00:07:59.378
to try to prosecute, prosecute.

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:01.647
Russian military units,

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:02.482
we're probably going

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:04.350
to see
more of this coming from

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.452
just the Ukrainian judicial system

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:08.521
in the months and years ahead.

